00:18:20.216 --> 00:18:22.720
which I'm now realizing you hate.

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.711
(all laugh)

00:18:25.711 --> 00:18:28.324
- [Jill] Gonna get to that
Kevin Love conversation.

00:18:28.324 --> 00:18:30.756
- Yeah, playing like
pickup games at school

00:18:30.756 --> 00:18:33.919
and playing in middle school on the team.

00:18:35.076 --> 00:18:36.016
- I appreciate it, Beanz.

00:18:36.016 --> 00:18:38.016
So, what are the challenges?

00:18:38.016 --> 00:18:39.459
Let's just break it down.

00:18:40.837 --> 00:18:42.526
I'll DJ Beanz's question,

00:18:42.526 --> 00:18:44.496
'cause I'm curious for myself actually.

00:18:44.496 --> 00:18:48.296
When it was at its best
moments, highest reigning stars,

00:18:48.296 --> 00:18:51.956
white heat moment, 'cause I
don't think you're at your down

00:18:51.956 --> 00:18:53.966
right now, especially when
I look at it historically,

00:18:53.966 --> 00:18:56.516
but in comparison to
your white heat moment,

00:18:56.516 --> 00:18:57.796
what were the challenges then,

00:18:57.796 --> 00:19:00.206
and what are the current
challenges in your perspective?

00:19:00.206 --> 00:19:01.836
- Yeah, I think that challenges,

00:19:01.836 --> 00:19:04.403
I think there were a lot of
opportunities in the '90s,

00:19:04.403 --> 00:19:06.986
and there was kind of
an explosion of NASCAR.

00:19:06.986 --> 00:19:08.676
A lot of it had to do with

00:19:08.676 --> 00:19:13.566
taking what was considered
to be a Southern sport

00:19:13.566 --> 00:19:15.166
and expanding across the country.

00:19:15.166 --> 00:19:17.436
- Yeah, Beanz, just to give you context,

00:19:17.436 --> 00:19:19.616
back in the day, this was like,

00:19:19.616 --> 00:19:21.419
oh that's that country thing.

00:19:22.806 --> 00:19:26.906
It was a very specific geographic.

00:19:26.906 --> 00:19:28.946
By the way, just to put into context,

00:19:28.946 --> 00:19:31.576
no different than lacrosse
was a Northeast thing,

00:19:31.576 --> 00:19:32.826
there's a lot of these things.

00:19:32.826 --> 00:19:34.879
Surfing, nobody's surfing in Oklahoma.

00:19:36.246 --> 00:19:39.926
There's a lot of that, but
it was, as a huge sport,

00:19:39.926 --> 00:19:42.436
it was unbelievably regional.

00:19:42.436 --> 00:19:46.216
- I agree, so I think there
were different challenges,

00:19:46.216 --> 00:19:47.536
there were media challenges,

00:19:47.536 --> 00:19:52.536
because NASCAR races were
on 12, 13 different--

00:19:53.826 --> 00:19:55.281
- Networks?
- Networks.

00:19:55.281 --> 00:19:56.716
- And reconsolidated the media deal.

00:19:56.716 --> 00:19:58.453
- Media rights in '01.

00:20:00.336 --> 00:20:02.846
But just kind of the expansion

00:20:02.846 --> 00:20:04.196
in this country.
- Was NASCAR's first

00:20:04.196 --> 00:20:07.086
national boost Worldwide of Sports?

00:20:07.086 --> 00:20:09.396
That's where I, as a real young kid,

00:20:09.396 --> 00:20:11.326
and probably happening even before I was,

00:20:11.326 --> 00:20:12.926
that's probably why I know Petty.

00:20:12.926 --> 00:20:15.996
It feels like Worldwide
of Sports, was that?

00:20:15.996 --> 00:20:17.308
Or Daytona 500?

00:20:17.308 --> 00:20:18.141
- I think Daytona 500.

00:20:18.141 --> 00:20:21.626
So the '79 Daytona 500,
there was snowstorm.

00:20:21.626 --> 00:20:24.706
Big fight.
- Oh, right, I remember that!

00:20:24.706 --> 00:20:27.016
- Punches being thrown, brothers involved,

00:20:27.016 --> 00:20:29.326
it was like the seminal moment.

00:20:29.326 --> 00:20:31.329
- It made evening news from everywhere?

00:20:32.966 --> 00:20:36.946
America's like wait, those
fuckers fight on the track?

00:20:36.946 --> 00:20:38.926
- It was the first live broadcast as well,

00:20:38.926 --> 00:20:41.336
so a lot of things came together.

00:20:41.336 --> 00:20:42.756
- Was the fight staged?

00:20:42.756 --> 00:20:43.686
- No.
- It was not.

00:20:43.686 --> 00:20:44.686
- [Gary] That would've been way better.

00:20:44.686 --> 00:20:48.816
- Our drivers get pissed.
- They were just pissed.

00:20:48.816 --> 00:20:51.446
They put the helmet on, their
brain leaks out the side.

00:20:51.446 --> 00:20:52.546
- They still fucking jump out

00:20:52.546 --> 00:20:54.756
and throw their helmet at each other.

00:20:54.756 --> 00:20:56.716
Tony Stewart was great for that stuff.

00:20:56.716 --> 00:20:58.010
- [Jill] Really good.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:59.399
- He was angry a lot.

00:21:00.286 --> 00:21:01.636
- Yeah, that's how he rolled.

00:21:01.636 --> 00:21:03.086
So, that was a challenge, what about now?

00:21:03.086 --> 00:21:03.956
- So I think now,

00:21:03.956 --> 00:21:07.866
we've certainly got a number of challenges

00:21:07.866 --> 00:21:08.786
that we're overcoming.

00:21:08.786 --> 00:21:11.616
I think the retirement
thing was certainly,

00:21:11.616 --> 00:21:12.793
but I think just people--

00:21:12.793 --> 00:21:14.136
- Was the TV switch, right,

00:21:14.136 --> 00:21:17.366
'cause Fox was your big play
in that white heat moment,

00:21:17.366 --> 00:21:18.489
and I don't recall.

00:21:20.546 --> 00:21:23.066
- So, we had Fox, and
then we had NBC, TNT,

00:21:23.066 --> 00:21:27.841
and then we had switched back to ESPN,

00:21:27.841 --> 00:21:30.136
and then we are now Fox and NBC.

00:21:30.136 --> 00:21:32.436
So, we had great media partners,

00:21:32.436 --> 00:21:34.246
but I think it's people's time,

00:21:34.246 --> 00:21:36.376
we need to make sure that we're relevant,

00:21:36.376 --> 00:21:40.476
and so that's why the
changes to the racing itself,

00:21:40.476 --> 00:21:42.646
because we want it to be
as exciting as it can be,

00:21:42.646 --> 00:21:46.166
so we want a race at the
tracks that people wanna go to,

00:21:46.166 --> 00:21:48.216
to see the racing that we wanna see,

00:21:48.216 --> 00:21:51.086
we want close competitive
side-by-side racing,

00:21:51.086 --> 00:21:53.536
guys mixing it up on the track,

00:21:53.536 --> 00:21:56.186
and in some cases, off the track.

00:21:56.186 --> 00:21:59.569
But people's time is valuable.

00:22:00.776 --> 00:22:03.316
- And you better have a
compelling story to break through,

00:22:03.316 --> 00:22:04.186
'cause there's so much.

00:22:04.186 --> 00:22:06.836
- When I look at how
much time is being spent

00:22:06.836 --> 00:22:08.796
watching my videos on YouTube,

00:22:08.796 --> 00:22:11.416
the first thing I always
go to, I'm like, my God,

00:22:11.416 --> 00:22:15.946
20 years ago, that was going
into TV shows, magazines.

00:22:15.946 --> 00:22:17.899
That's one little me, just me.

00:22:18.903 --> 00:22:19.896
And you start thinking--

00:22:19.896 --> 00:22:22.986
- I agree, so you take a look
at television ratings, right?

00:22:22.986 --> 00:22:26.882
So, our TV ratings this
year, all sports down 9%,

00:22:26.882 --> 00:22:29.746
just fewer people watching television.

00:22:29.746 --> 00:22:31.026
- [Gary] Yeah, the end.

00:22:31.026 --> 00:22:33.516
- Cord Cutters, Never Cords, Cord Shavers,

00:22:33.516 --> 00:22:34.656
