00:22:34.656 --> 00:22:38.286
- Or a generation, my
little guy, six-year-old,

00:22:38.286 --> 00:22:41.556
would rather watch a
baseball game on his iPad

00:22:41.556 --> 00:22:43.696
with updated moments.

00:22:43.696 --> 00:22:46.916
He has it on, but he only
watches it on the iPad,

00:22:46.916 --> 00:22:51.816
'cause he likes to see all
the data around the at-bat.

00:22:51.816 --> 00:22:54.026
The game is literally
on, he's not watching it,

00:22:54.026 --> 00:22:57.246
'cause he's watching in
realtime on the iPad.

00:22:57.246 --> 00:23:01.266
- So, you're adapting to changing needs,

00:23:01.266 --> 00:23:02.116
and we're doing the same thing.

00:23:02.116 --> 00:23:05.806
So, for us, our ratings
this year were plus three,

00:23:05.806 --> 00:23:08.696
so are we back and killing it?

00:23:08.696 --> 00:23:11.626
We're coming back, and
we're onto something,

00:23:11.626 --> 00:23:13.026
and it's that young drivers.

00:23:14.741 --> 00:23:18.129
- And with fewer people
watching TV in general.

00:23:18.129 --> 00:23:20.866
- [Gary] Beanz, I appreciate the call.

00:23:20.866 --> 00:23:23.316
