fans or hardcore soccer fans,

00:23:32.796 --> 00:23:34.756
do you ever take the
time to try to convert,

00:23:34.756 --> 00:23:36.326
or are you just really focused

00:23:36.326 --> 00:23:38.846
on the people who already like NASCAR?

00:23:38.846 --> 00:23:41.196
- The Beanz part of your
question was just okay,

00:23:41.196 --> 00:23:43.543
the Rice part of your
question was amazing.

00:23:43.543 --> 00:23:45.936
(all laugh)

00:23:45.936 --> 00:23:48.776
- So, I'll take this,
and Jill can jump in.

00:23:48.776 --> 00:23:53.776
I think we wanna convert people...

00:23:55.716 --> 00:23:57.086
where there's fertile ground, right?

00:23:57.086 --> 00:24:00.916
So, if someone is just into basketball,

00:24:00.916 --> 00:24:03.816
we have a ton of crossover
with other sports,

00:24:03.816 --> 00:24:05.946
so believe it or not, there
are folks that watch golf

00:24:05.946 --> 00:24:07.696
that also love NASCAR.

00:24:07.696 --> 00:24:09.056
- [Gary] That makes a lot
of sense to me, actually.

00:24:09.056 --> 00:24:12.835
- The biggest crossover
for us actually is the NFL.

00:24:12.835 --> 00:24:13.668
- [Gary] That also makes sense.

00:24:13.668 --> 00:24:15.626
- That crossover for us is huge.

00:24:15.626 --> 00:24:17.056
- What about college football,
or you don't score that?

00:24:17.056 --> 00:24:17.889
- [Steve] College football for sure.

00:24:17.889 --> 00:24:19.866
- To me, that feels super intuitive,

00:24:19.866 --> 00:24:22.631
the epicenter of college
football sits in a demo--

00:24:22.631 --> 00:24:24.616
- In the Southeast, no question.

00:24:24.616 --> 00:24:26.702
For us, we need to make sure--

00:24:26.702 --> 00:24:29.276
- [Gary] Is that Beanz?

00:24:29.276 --> 00:24:30.866
- [India] I don't think so.

00:24:30.866 --> 00:24:32.806
- That we're nurturing
the folks that we have,

00:24:32.806 --> 00:24:35.516
'cause we wanna keep that hardcore fan,

00:24:35.516 --> 00:24:40.116
but then we need to find this
younger, more diverse fan,

00:24:40.116 --> 00:24:41.363
and we're working hard

00:24:41.363 --> 00:24:42.196
to do that.
- Any sport

00:24:42.196 --> 00:24:44.456
that isn't thinking
about youth and diversity

00:24:44.456 --> 00:24:47.116
is looking to not win 2030.

00:24:47.116 --> 00:24:49.326
- [Jill] And storylines matter, right?

00:24:49.326 --> 00:24:50.616
People want storylines.

00:24:50.616 --> 00:24:52.596
- [Gary] And you wanna see
somebody that looks like you.

00:24:52.596 --> 00:24:53.429
- That's exactly right.

00:24:53.429 --> 00:24:55.686
- The best thing to happen to
baseball was Jackie Robinson.

00:24:55.686 --> 00:24:57.186
I mean, anyway, let's move on.

00:24:58.636 --> 00:25:00.476
It's really cool, it's
really interesting to me,

00:25:00.476 --> 00:25:03.476
because also one thing that I think

00:25:03.476 --> 00:25:05.226
people are starting to
understand, because of Esports,

00:25:05.226 --> 00:25:06.716
and really, let's call it what it is,

00:25:06.716 --> 00:25:09.519
the growth of, go ahead.

00:25:10.526 --> 00:25:14.429
The growth of proper
football, soccer, in America,

00:25:16.486 --> 00:25:18.936
it's really interesting
to understand that, good?

00:25:20.069 --> 00:25:21.236
- [Jill On Recording]
And storylines matter.

00:25:21.236 --> 00:25:22.143
- Hey, Beanz.

00:25:23.066 --> 00:25:24.146
- [Beanz] Hey, thank you.

00:25:24.146 --> 00:25:24.996
- You're welcome.

00:25:26.250 --> 00:25:28.666
