you're on The #AskGaryVee Show

00:25:56.693 --> 00:25:58.696
with the NASCAR crew.
- All right, Gary Vee!

00:25:58.696 --> 00:26:00.076
How are you today?

00:26:00.076 --> 00:26:02.466
- I'm well, say hello to the NASCAR crew.

00:26:02.466 --> 00:26:04.026
- [Steven] Yeah, how you doing, Steve,

00:26:04.026 --> 00:26:05.466
how you doing, Jill?

00:26:05.466 --> 00:26:07.476
- [Jill] Doing great, how are you, Steven?

00:26:07.476 --> 00:26:10.376
- [Steven] Well, I think
you made a great segue

00:26:10.376 --> 00:26:12.696
into my question, it's
talking about Esports there,

00:26:12.696 --> 00:26:16.296
Gary Vee, so we got a driver
right now, William Byron,

00:26:16.296 --> 00:26:18.406
driver of the number 24 car,

00:26:18.406 --> 00:26:21.816
who made his start in racing in E-racing,

00:26:21.816 --> 00:26:24.366
and you got a big event this week on NBC

00:26:24.366 --> 00:26:27.436
where you televise iRacing, E-racing,

00:26:27.436 --> 00:26:29.316
for the very first time.

00:26:29.316 --> 00:26:31.616
What does the sport, the future of that,

00:26:31.616 --> 00:26:33.559
look like for NASCAR?

00:26:34.482 --> 00:26:36.469
- [Gary] That's a great question.

00:26:36.469 --> 00:26:37.302
- Go ahead.

00:26:37.302 --> 00:26:38.513
- Go ahead, Jill.

00:26:38.513 --> 00:26:39.786
- It's a great question.

00:26:39.786 --> 00:26:41.946
I think that the fact that William Byron

00:26:41.946 --> 00:26:45.286
sat on the pole the Daytona
500, and did no racing

00:26:45.286 --> 00:26:46.526
until he did iRacing,

00:26:46.526 --> 00:26:49.746
which was our simulated Esports product,

00:26:49.746 --> 00:26:51.326
is a story that hasn't been told.

00:26:51.326 --> 00:26:52.159
You could start

00:26:52.159 --> 00:26:53.389
doing that today
- That's an insane story.

00:26:53.389 --> 00:26:56.166
- And that's the pinnacle of our sport.

00:26:56.166 --> 00:26:58.216
- I'm not sure there is another sport

00:26:58.216 --> 00:26:59.496
that will have that happen.

00:26:59.496 --> 00:27:00.836
- [Jill] You can't go play Madden

00:27:00.836 --> 00:27:02.306
and then go play for the Jets.

00:27:02.306 --> 00:27:03.526
Well, maybe you could play for the Jets.

00:27:03.526 --> 00:27:05.276
- No, you're right, I mean I wish I could,

00:27:05.276 --> 00:27:06.826
I'm not good enough for Madden either.

00:27:06.826 --> 00:27:11.686
No, that's right, that
is actually remarkable.

00:27:11.686 --> 00:27:14.906
And like actually, look, I
think that soccer matters

00:27:14.906 --> 00:27:16.276
in America 'cause of FIFA.

00:27:16.276 --> 00:27:20.266
I was there when the first FIFA
Sega Genesis game came out.

00:27:20.266 --> 00:27:22.756
And I bought it, 'cause I bought
all video games back then,

00:27:22.756 --> 00:27:24.546
and none of my friends wanted to play,

00:27:24.546 --> 00:27:27.966
'cause nobody gave a shit
about soccer in 1994.

00:27:27.966 --> 00:27:29.486
And then slowly but surely,

00:27:29.486 --> 00:27:32.219
FIFA got bigger and bigger and bigger.

00:27:33.615 --> 00:27:35.856
I mean, but again, back to that point,

00:27:35.856 --> 00:27:38.706
you're not playing for
Liverpool after being awesome.

00:27:38.706 --> 00:27:40.856
The fact that you guys have that

00:27:40.856 --> 00:27:43.306
might actually be the singular unlock.

00:27:43.306 --> 00:27:44.926
- Well, and I think the
hardest thing for us

00:27:44.926 --> 00:27:47.116
is you can't go play
NASCAR in the backyard.

00:27:47.116 --> 00:27:49.516
- Back to the guy who said basketball,

00:27:49.516 --> 00:27:50.349
I was thinking that.

00:27:50.349 --> 00:27:51.182
- Exactly.

00:27:51.182 --> 00:27:53.916
So, this is a way that you can participate

00:27:53.916 --> 00:27:56.126
and understand how our sport works

00:27:56.126 --> 00:27:57.346
and get to be good at it

00:27:57.346 --> 00:27:59.336
without having to go to a racetrack.

00:27:59.336 --> 00:28:01.046
We want everybody to come to races.

00:28:01.046 --> 00:28:01.879
- Jill, I apologize.

00:28:01.879 --> 00:28:04.216
Did you guys think that
that was gonna happen

00:28:04.216 --> 00:28:05.636
when you first rolled out the program,

00:28:05.636 --> 00:28:08.426
or was that even too big
of a leap for you guys

00:28:08.426 --> 00:28:11.506
that somebody's gonna sit
at home, get great at this,

00:28:11.506 --> 00:28:13.356
and then actually be a fucking player?

00:28:13.356 --> 00:28:14.189
- Well, I don't think

00:28:14.189 --> 00:28:15.966
we could've never scripted that ourselves.

00:28:15.966 --> 00:28:17.259
We get accused of
scripting a lot of things.

00:28:17.259 --> 00:28:19.926
- Did you believe that
that was gonna happen?

00:28:19.926 --> 00:28:21.977
- No, no way.

00:28:21.977 --> 00:28:22.973
- I did not.

00:28:22.973 --> 00:28:25.276
- And he's driving Jeff Gordon's car,

00:28:25.276 --> 00:28:26.926
this kid, William Byron,

00:28:26.926 --> 00:28:31.926
who we know was doing nothing at age 15,

00:28:32.116 --> 00:28:33.296
picked up iRacing.

00:28:33.296 --> 00:28:34.346
Nothing in the sport.

00:28:35.386 --> 00:28:37.006
He's a great kid.

00:28:37.006 --> 00:28:39.146
And he's driving one
of the most iconic cars

00:28:39.146 --> 00:28:41.356
at the highest level, and so I think that

00:28:41.356 --> 00:28:43.016
the more people that understand

00:28:43.016 --> 00:28:44.209
and get exposed to NASCAR through iRacing.

00:28:44.209 --> 00:28:46.286
- Jill, I'll be very honest with you,

00:28:46.286 --> 00:28:47.682
I'm not sure I made the connection point

00:28:47.682 --> 00:28:49.666
to the question, Steven,
thank you for asking.

00:28:49.666 --> 00:28:51.866
I actually think that's
the complete unlock.

00:28:52.846 --> 00:28:53.886
It's crazy!

00:28:53.886 --> 00:28:56.116
That will capture the imagination

00:28:56.116 --> 00:28:58.489
of an enormous amount of girls and boys.

00:28:59.586 --> 00:29:02.306
The only place you can go

00:29:02.306 --> 00:29:06.837
from video game to actual
profession is NASCAR.

00:29:06.837 --> 00:29:07.816
I actually think that's true.

00:29:07.816 --> 00:29:09.906
- Well, I think that the
other component to that too,

00:29:09.906 --> 00:29:10.739
and Jill alluded to it,

00:29:10.739 --> 00:29:12.596
you can't go in the backyard to do it,

00:29:13.466 --> 00:29:15.793
but you can do it online,
and you can do iRacing,

00:29:15.793 --> 00:29:19.206
and it is incredible simulated racing.

00:29:19.206 --> 00:29:20.646
- Well, clearly, that's the point

00:29:20.646 --> 00:29:22.176
that I didn't make the connection on,

00:29:22.176 --> 00:29:25.806
which is the product is so good

00:29:25.806 --> 00:29:27.916
that the mapping of being great at it

00:29:27.916 --> 00:29:30.896
maps enough to real life, that's nuts!

00:29:30.896 --> 00:29:33.546
- Well, I think the nice
thing about it too is,

00:29:33.546 --> 00:29:35.646
car racing is expensive,

00:29:35.646 --> 00:29:38.916
and so you can figure out early and often

00:29:38.916 --> 00:29:40.306
whether you're good at it or not,

00:29:40.306 --> 00:29:42.971
so you're not spending 10s
of thousands of dollars.

00:29:42.971 --> 00:29:45.076
- I've always thought that this
was hockey's biggest issue,

00:29:45.076 --> 00:29:47.676
it's expensive to be in youth hockey,

00:29:47.676 --> 00:29:49.206
which eliminates a lot of great athletes

00:29:49.206 --> 00:29:51.186
from ever getting into the pipe.

00:29:51.186 --> 00:29:54.126
- And the fact that NBC
is gonna broadcast it,

00:29:54.126 --> 00:29:56.043
I mean, that's gonna be
huge exposure for it,

00:29:56.043 --> 00:29:58.806
and that's Steven's question is that

00:29:58.806 --> 00:30:00.276
the fact that our media partners

00:30:00.276 --> 00:30:02.796
are taking this component
of NASCAR seriously

00:30:02.796 --> 00:30:06.459
is gonna be even bigger and
expose more people to it.

00:30:08.276 --> 00:30:10.296
- Steven, I appreciate the question.

00:30:10.296 --> 00:30:11.129
- [Steven] Yep, no problem!

00:30:11.129 --> 00:30:11.986
Thank you very much!

00:30:11.986 --> 00:30:13.596
- Thanks for watching the show.

00:30:13.596 --> 00:30:14.546
All right, let's get one more in.

00:30:14.546 --> 00:30:15.506
That was a great question.

00:30:15.506 --> 00:30:17.156
- [Jill] Yeah, it was really good.

00:30:17.156 --> 00:30:18.326
- I really gotta tell you,

00:30:18.326 --> 00:30:20.176
I think there's something real there.

00:30:22.426 --> 00:30:23.866
I think that's something that you have

00:30:23.866 --> 00:30:27.079
that is so much of an advantage
compared to any other sport.

00:30:27.916 --> 00:30:29.386
- I agree, well, I think
the other thing too

00:30:29.386 --> 00:30:31.866
is the people that do iRacing,

00:30:31.866 --> 00:30:36.209
they're absolutely nuts about
it, that's the cool thing.

00:30:37.786 --> 00:30:39.351
- [India] Guitars Ruin Lives.

00:30:39.351 --> 00:30:40.438
- Excuse me?

00:30:40.438 --> 00:30:42.189
- Guitars Ruin Lives, but he plays guitar.

