00:30:58.746 --> 00:30:59.586
Thank you guys.

00:30:59.586 --> 00:31:00.419
- No worries.

00:31:00.419 --> 00:31:01.756
What's your question?

00:31:01.756 --> 00:31:02.589
- [Josh] So, the question,

00:31:02.589 --> 00:31:04.906
as I put it forth in the comments there,

00:31:04.906 --> 00:31:08.796
was I think it's interesting
looking at sponsorship

00:31:08.796 --> 00:31:11.706
as something, I'm no huge NASCAR fan,

00:31:11.706 --> 00:31:13.486
so I'm not posing here, but at least,

00:31:13.486 --> 00:31:14.926
everybody's familiar with the concept

00:31:14.926 --> 00:31:17.726
of the patches being on
them and all that stuff,

00:31:17.726 --> 00:31:22.636
and I imagine there's a
lot that has gone into that

00:31:22.636 --> 00:31:27.414
as far as drivers and their promoters,

00:31:27.414 --> 00:31:30.186
their managers, marketing,

00:31:30.186 --> 00:31:33.846
and using that as a
cross-pollination thing culturally,

00:31:33.846 --> 00:31:36.471
and business-wise, of course,
trying to drive business,

00:31:36.471 --> 00:31:39.376
and I think it's
interesting looking at that

00:31:39.376 --> 00:31:42.276
compared to influencer culture

00:31:42.276 --> 00:31:43.446
and all the things that you talk about

00:31:43.446 --> 00:31:46.779
as far as damning and
whether you're looking at it

00:31:46.779 --> 00:31:49.796
from the business angle of a
business using a small service

00:31:49.796 --> 00:31:52.676
to promote their agenda or vice versa,

00:31:52.676 --> 00:31:54.296
I think that's fascinating, so I'm curious

00:31:54.296 --> 00:31:56.766
if your guests could speak a little bit

00:31:56.766 --> 00:31:58.216
to that kind of model,

00:31:58.216 --> 00:32:01.356
and I guess you could
speak to how that relates

00:32:01.356 --> 00:32:03.499
to what influencers should be doing today.

00:32:05.286 --> 00:32:06.919
- Well, I think for our drivers,

00:32:08.486 --> 00:32:11.286
the sponsors can be in the field of play,

00:32:11.286 --> 00:32:13.756
the sponsors are their personal partners,

00:32:13.756 --> 00:32:15.876
so it's not slapping a logo on a uniform

00:32:15.876 --> 00:32:17.776
or getting a personal services agreement;

00:32:17.776 --> 00:32:21.466
they are in the fabric of
what makes these drivers tick,

00:32:21.466 --> 00:32:25.976
so I think for us, we've
gotta pay attention to that.

00:32:25.976 --> 00:32:30.546
I think where we also kind
of struggle a little bit--

00:32:30.546 --> 00:32:31.636
- You mean some of the sponsors

00:32:31.636 --> 00:32:33.246
are actually integrated into the product,

00:32:33.246 --> 00:32:34.156
but some aren't, right?

00:32:34.156 --> 00:32:35.236
- [Jill] No, they aren't, but they are--

00:32:35.236 --> 00:32:37.466
- Like the M&amp;M's car,

00:32:37.466 --> 00:32:38.586
the most integrated it can be

00:32:38.586 --> 00:32:41.426
is he or she is eating
the M&amp;M's during the race.

00:32:41.426 --> 00:32:43.026
- Yeah, which may happen.

00:32:43.026 --> 00:32:45.306
Dick Trickle used to have
candy in his car, right?

00:32:45.306 --> 00:32:47.356
We know the Dick Trickle story.

00:32:47.356 --> 00:32:50.796
But your brand is on the
car, your brand is on,

00:32:50.796 --> 00:32:51.753
very few brands are on the field.

00:32:51.753 --> 00:32:55.346
- And even the NBA, which
has gotten progressive,

